          </h2>

          <p>
            Penetrating driveway sealers typically cover about 100 to 200 square feet per gallon per coat on broom-finished concrete, and most driveway applications use two coats or a wet-on-wet flood coat. Porous, older concrete drinks more; dense new concrete takes less. Check the current label for your product's range and plan to the lower number.
          </p>

