          </p>

          <p>
            Film-forming acrylics and urethanes still have a place. They are the only way to get a wet look or strong color enhancement, and they block oil better than penetrating repellents do. On stamped, colored or exposed-aggregate driveways, many owners accept the recoating cycle in exchange for the appearance. On plain broom-finished gray concrete, the case for a film is weak.
