        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For a plain concrete driveway in a cold, salted climate, buy a silane-siloxane penetrating sealer and put it on before the first frost. Ghostshield Siloxa-Tek 8500 is the top choice for heavy salt exposure, Foundation Armor SX5000 WB is the easiest ready-to-use option, and Eagle Natural Seal covers a tight budget. On older, dusty slabs, densify first with a lithium silicate and then apply the repellent.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Choose a film sealer only for decorative concrete, and accept the recoats and grit additive that come with it. Then do the small things every year: keep joints filled, use deicers sparingly, avoid ammonium-based products, and test with water each fall. Those habits add years to a driveway.
